# Scientific Review Checklist

## Research-intent alignment

- Existing S1-S5 scenarios are used where required.
- Every primary topology-producing method uses K<=2.
- Unconstrained variants are excluded from the main comparison.
- Stage I-a and Stage I-b retain distinct intended roles.
- TH and AH are represented as heuristic comparison methods.
- AC projection is applied only to selected finalists.
- GridFM and DC projection objectives use intended anchors.

## Power-system physics

- Canonical physical branches are used.
- Duplicate directed GridFM edges are not independent topology decisions.
- Offline lines have zero flow.
- DC nodal balance, generator limits, load-service bounds, and branch thermal limits are enforced.
- Transformer taps and phase shifts are handled or explicitly verified trivial.
- Source-less islands cannot appear falsely served.
- DC feasibility is not described as AC feasibility.
- GridFM predictions are not described as verified AC solutions.
- Projection distance is not confused with a residual.

## Mathematical consistency

- Objective weights are applied consistently.
- Shared risk denominator matches stored-scenario baseline definition.
- Load shedding is demand-weighted.
- Stage I-a and Stage I-b objectives match documentation.
- DC rows are not falsely assigned GridFM PAC semantics.
- Target recall and precision use correct denominators.

## Experimental fairness

- Same scenarios, candidate-line universe where intended, topology budget, lambda sweep, shared normalization, and target definitions.
- Solver failures and projection failures remain visible.
- Time-limited MIQP rows are labeled.
- Heuristic points do not exceed shutdown budget.

## Literature alignment

- TH/AH/MLD definitions should be checked against provided literature once the literature library is populated.
